From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 04:30:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec: add V4L2 Request API MPEG-4 Part 2 and H.263 hwaccel

Stateless MPEG-4 Part 2 Simple and Advanced Simple profile and H.263
baseline decoding through the private MPEG-4 controls Cedrus takes: a
request per video packet, per H.263 GOB with a header, or per VOP when
the stream has neither.

FFmpeg hands the hwaccel the whole VOP once, so the packets are found
here: a resync marker sits byte-aligned and cannot be emulated, a GOB
start code may sit at any bit. Each run of macroblocks is queued as
soon as the next header is found, the last one at the end of the frame.

The VOL is the init probe: a driver refusing its tools fails the init
and decoding falls back to software. So do tools the controls cannot
carry: shapes, NEWPRED, scalability, the H.263 annexes, and interlaced
streams that may carry B-VOPs, which Cedrus refuses.
---
